# Every environment variable portfolio-ops reads, with its tier and where its value comes
# from (REPO-BASELINE.md §2). None is always required: validate and report run without any.
#
# To use them locally, copy this file to .env — gitignored, like every *.env — fill in
# what you need, and load it into your shell:
#
#     set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# Never commit a real value. The pre-commit hook and CI scan every commit for secrets.

# GITHUB_TOKEN
#   Tier: optional locally; provided by GitHub Actions in CI.
#   Needed for `portfolio-ops report --publish` (without --dry-run); --dry-run reads the
#   open weekly-review issues with it when it is set. Locally, a fine-grained token with
#   "Issues: read and write" on the data repository is enough. In GitHub Actions the
#   workflow's own token is passed through the action's github-token input, and the
#   visibility guard (rule S7) uses it too. Never printed or logged.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# GITHUB_REPOSITORY
#   Tier: optional; not a secret. Set by GitHub Actions in CI.
#   OWNER/NAME of the data repository that --publish writes to when --repo is not given.
GITHUB_REPOSITORY=
